content.text:
Result screen looks good except the subtitle currently Latin digits (will be fixed after reload). The score pips: 4 diamonds, 2 orange at right, 2 dark at left. Because RTL, P1 pips on the right; clear enough. The title color is gold, nice.

However, the timer in HUD shows "۶۶" (?) and the round pips at top are blurred. Fine.

The subtitle order "نتیجه نهایی 2 — 0" visually reads 2-0, P1 score first. With Persian digits and RTL bidi, `نتیجه نهایی ۲ — ۰` may render as "نتیجه نهایی ۲ — ۰" with ۲ on the right? Bidi reorders; in the screenshot with Latin digits it displays "0 — 2" visually? Wait screenshot shows "نتیجه نهایی 2 — 0"?? Looking at image: text below title reads "نتیجه نهایی 2 — 0" (2 on left, 0 on right?) Actually it's hard to parse. The template `${score[0]} — ${score[1]}` = "2 — 0". In RTL context, bidi renders the Latin digits left-to-right as "2 — 0", but the phrase is at center; in the image it looks like "2 — 0" with 2 left. P1 won 2, and visually the winner's score should probably appear on the right (Persian start side). With `toFa`, bidi may treat Persian digits as weak LTR too. So still "۲ — ۰" left-to-right. That's fine; standard score format is winner first.

The pause button etc.

Now after reload, result screen test would need repeating, but the change is trivial.

Now fix the round pips maybe? They look okay. The top HUD timer localized; good.

Next, I want to improve the **mobile landscape** controls overlay so the labels and buttons are readable and don't cover the fighters too much. In landscape 844x390, the stage 693x390 centered; controls occupy bottom ~110px. Fighters at y 606/720*390=328 and their heads at ~170; buttons overlap feet only. That's fine. The HUD meter bars at y=664/720*390=360 are hidden behind the control clusters; but special readiness is also indicated by portrait glow and the "ضربه نهایی آماده!" text at bottom, which is hidden. On mobile, players won't know when super is ready except via portrait glow (subtle) or by trying. This could be improved by making the touch super button visually light up when meter >=100. Not bound, but we can add a simple check in the render loop or in main loop to update classes based on fighter meter. Since meter changes every frame, add in main.js after game.update or in frameLoop: toggle a class on touch controls based on game.fighters[0].meter etc. This is a nice touch and improves mobile UX.

Implementation:
- In `frameLoop`, after updates, call `syncTouchState()` (or only every ~6 frames).
- Get buttons: `.touch-side.p1 .abtn.a4`, `.p2 .abtn.a4`; add class `ready` if meter >=100; also maybe `.a3` if >=25.
- Add CSS for `.abtn.ready` pulsing glow.
- CPU mode P2 hidden, fine.
- Also maybe disable/visually dim unusable special/super buttons when meter < requirement. This helps players understand. Add classes `.locked` when insufficient meter; CSS opacity .55. But if dimmed, they still respond; no issue. Use `disabled`? No, don't disable because pointerup might stick; keep clickable. Visual only.
- Since touch buttons exist on desktop? hidden but DOM; fine.

Add `syncTouchMeter` function in main.js:
```
const p1Super = touchControls.querySelector('.touch-side.p1 .abtn.a4');
...
function syncTouchMeter() {
  for (const [id, side] of [[0, '.p1'], [1, '.p2']]) {
    const f = game.fighters[id];
    const a4 = ...
    a4.classList.toggle('ready', f.meter >= 100);
    a3.classList.toggle('locked', f.meter < 25);
    a4.classList.toggle('locked', f.meter < 100);
  }
}
```
Call in frameLoop every frame (cheap). CSS:
```
.abtn.a3.locked, .abtn.a4.locked { opacity: .45; }
.abtn.a4.ready { border-color: #ffe6a0; box-shadow: 0 0 18px ...; animation: super-pulse 1s infinite; }
```
Note `.abtn.a4.ready` should override player-specific borders; add specificity `.p1 .abtn.a4.ready` etc. Simpler: `.abtn.ready { animation; filter: brightness(1.3); } .abtn.a4.ready { box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(255,220,130,.75), inset 0 0 16px rgba(255,215,110,.5); border-color: rgba(255,225,150,.9); }` This overrides p1/p2 border due to same specificity? `.abtn.a4.ready` specificity (0,3,0) vs `.p1 .abtn.a4` (0,3,0) and comes later → wins if written after. Good.

Also maybe show a tiny meter ring around the attack button? Overkill.

Let's implement.

